            ("If a firm's Cost of Goods Sold is GH₵ 240,000 and average inventory held is GH₵ 40,000, what is its inventory turnover rate?", ["6 times per year", "4 times per year", "8 times per year", "12 times per year"], 0, "Inventory turnover = 240,000 / 40,000 = 6 times per annum.", "Financial Ratio Calculations"),
            ("The Trade Receivables Collection Period measures:", ["The average number of days it takes for credit customers to settle their invoices", "The time taken to purchase inventory", "The frequency of bank audits", "The lifespan of delivery trucks"], 0, "Debtors Collection Period = (Trade Receivables / Credit Sales) × 365 days.", "Liquidity Management"),
