            ("If a firm sells goods costing GH₵ 60,000 with a mark-up of 25% on cost, what is the selling price?", ["GH₵ 75,000", "GH₵ 80,000", "GH₵ 72,000", "GH₵ 65,000"], 0, "Mark-up = 25% of 60,000 = 15,000. Selling Price = Cost + Mark-up = 60,000 + 15,000 = GH₵ 75,000.", "Margin and Mark-up"),
            ("A trader sells an article for GH₵ 100,000 achieving a gross margin of 20% on selling price. What was the cost of goods sold?", ["GH₵ 80,000", "GH₵ 83,333", "GH₵ 75,000", "GH₵ 90,000"], 0, "Gross profit = 20% of 100,000 = 20,000. Cost of goods sold = 100,000 - 20,000 = GH₵ 80,000.", "Commercial Arithmetic"),
            ("Which international accounting body issues International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS)?", ["International Accounting Standards Board (IASB)", "Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB)", "International Federation of Accountants (IFAC)", "United Nations Accounting Panel"], 0, "The IASB is the independent London-based body setting global IFRS reporting standards.", "Accounting Standards"),
            ("What is the primary role of external independent auditors in corporate financial reporting?", ["To express an objective professional opinion on whether financial statements show a true and fair view", "To prepare daily invoices for management", "To calculate employee tax deductions", "To manage company marketing campaigns"], 0, "Auditors test internal controls and examine accounts to provide reasonable assurance on financial statements.", "Auditing"),
