            ("In hire purchase accounting, the asset remains the legal property of the vendor until:", ["The final hire purchase installment and option fee are paid in full", "The initial down payment deposit is made", "The contract is signed", "Half the installments are cleared"], 0, "Hire purchase passes legal ownership only upon completion of all contractual installments.", "Hire Purchase"),
            ("The Hire Purchase Price of an asset is equal to:", ["Cash Price plus Total Hire Purchase Interest (Finance Charge)", "Cash Price minus Deposit", "Down payment multiplied by number of months", "Total installments minus cash price"], 0, "Hire purchase price reflects total cash outflow including financing interest charges.", "Hire Purchase"),
            ("Under the Two-Fold Aspect of accounting transactions, every financial transaction must affect:", ["At least two accounts in opposite directions (debit and credit)", "Only one account", "Three accounts simultaneously", "The balance sheet exclusively"], 0, "The dual aspect concept ensures total debits equal total credits across the accounting system.", "Accounting Principles"),
            ("Which financial ratio measures the proportion of a company's total capital structure funded by long-term debt versus equity?", ["Gearing Ratio (Leverage Ratio)", "Acid-Test Ratio", "Working Capital Ratio", "Gross Margin"], 0, "Gearing (Debt / [Debt + Equity]) evaluates financial risk and debt reliance.", "Capital Structure"),
